No, it’s not Barry Manilow. Here we’re talking about something way more badass – UK post-punk rockers create a raw and energetic garage sound with a distinctively British taste that reminds me of bands like Agent Orange, Wire, Television and The Sex Pistols.

![](https://scontent-a-lga.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xap1/v/t1.0-9/1560652_581596465254983_35898921_n.jpg?oh=cfeb9cd2fa43999f2503b28933a586a4&oe=54D72AEF)

The opening track “Missing” is as nihilistic and punk as it gets. The second track “Law Here” features sludgy guitars and languid vocals. I really like “Control Issue” with its high energy and oldschool vibe, which is the total opposite of the more laid back closing “Vitamins” with its long groovy guitar riffs.

{% embed provider="soundcloud" src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/playlists/51363559&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false&visual=true" /%}

Overall “Cease and Desist” is raw and even if it doesn’t really create something new, this debut EP possesses some of the best sides of the good old punk-rock. And what else do we need.

![](https://fbcdn-sphotos-e-a.akamaihd.net/hphotos-ak-xpa1/v/t1.0-9/10410846_713162485431713_7251895747230018611_n.jpg?oh=69145be049e2fa69eb2561c96fb99d7c&oe=54ED29CC&__gda__=1424704628_233658ef4fa135bc35ad276470a52163)

Manilow are Dean Moston, Paul Chamberlain and Gary Cardno. More about them on[Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/Manilow.band), [Soundcloud](https://soundcloud.com/manilow-band/) and [Bandcamp](https://manilow.bandcamp.com/).

